1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:05,478
Open Commerce, Campaigns.

2
00:00:05,478 --> 00:00:08,851
It lists your campaigns with their status:

3
00:00:08,851 --> 00:00:12,364
Draft, Scheduled, Sending, Sent or Canceled.

4
00:00:12,364 --> 00:00:14,120
Click Add campaign.

5
00:00:14,642 --> 00:00:16,077
Name the campaign.

6
00:00:16,077 --> 00:00:17,872
Only staff see the name.

7
00:00:17,872 --> 00:00:21,222
Choose its Segment, the customers who will get it.

8
00:00:21,699 --> 00:00:23,616
Write the Subject and the Email.

9
00:00:23,616 --> 00:00:26,491
The help under the field lists what you can put in:

10
00:00:26,491 --> 00:00:30,526
the customer's name, how many orders they placed and what they spent, your

11
00:00:30,526 --> 00:00:34,359
store's name, and their unsubscribe link, which is added at the end if

12
00:00:34,359 --> 00:00:35,519
you leave it out.

13
00:00:36,104 --> 00:00:40,690
To check it, enter your address under Send a test to, and click Send test.

14
00:00:40,690 --> 00:00:42,525
Nothing goes to customers:

15
00:00:42,525 --> 00:00:46,595
it is filled in as the segment's first customer would get it, and

16
00:00:46,595 --> 00:00:47,914
sent only to you.

17
00:00:48,371 --> 00:00:49,473
Click Send.

18
00:00:49,473 --> 00:00:54,075
Fill in Send at first to send it later, in your site's time zone.

19
00:00:54,075 --> 00:00:56,991
Or click Save draft to finish it later.

20
00:00:58,211 --> 00:01:02,590
A campaign goes out in batches over the next minutes, to the segment's

21
00:01:02,590 --> 00:01:05,414
customers as they are when each batch goes.

22
00:01:05,414 --> 00:01:09,217
Its page shows how many it was sent to, how many it skipped,

23
00:01:09,217 --> 00:01:13,884
because they have no email or do not accept marketing, and how many failed.

24
00:01:13,884 --> 00:01:15,901
Cancel the campaign stops it.

